{"chapter": "sites-cohomology", "node_kind": "section_title", "parent_tag": "0945", "placeholders": {}, "render": {"prefix": "\\section{", "suffix": "}\n\\label{section-w-contractible}"}, "risk_level": "R1", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:63dccb4c5097052dc30a817df195af3135aaf523506356c2e3813f6c94d81be8", "source_text": "Weakly contractible objects", "source_text_hash": "sha256:b85d6c428d034a5f7b702488bc05e45445e2a8eefbe915bbdc2d8b2135ebe01f", "unit_id": "tag:0945:title"}
{"chapter": "sites-cohomology", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "0945", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$U$", "MATH_0002": "$\\mathcal{F} \\to \\mathcal{G}$", "MATH_0003": "$\\mathcal{F}(U) \\to \\mathcal{G}(U)$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{sites-definition-w-contractible}", "STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent", "TEXTITCLOSE_0001": "}", "TEXTITOPEN_0001": "{\\it "}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:ea4cbfecc0a1dcce2926bb63fbb9bac5a17bd9b53ecc3a8544b4f914e5d6a4eb", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:2e590bacff269144c1ef95155d443a66d72d1a409d4f1eb736a894b6a28baa64", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nAn object <MATH_0001> of a site is <TEXTITOPEN_0001>weakly contractible<TEXTITCLOSE_0001> if every surjection\n<MATH_0002> of sheaves of sets gives rise to a surjection\n<MATH_0003>, see\nSites, Definition <REF_0001>.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:472d3120ab4cdf7cff134fb191c39ee930b0dedb8dbb245ee15bd5c3b7e83b23", "unit_id": "tag:0945:prose-0001"}
{"chapter": "sites-cohomology", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "0945", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$\\mathcal{C}$", "MATH_0002": "$U$", "MATH_0003": "$\\mathcal{C}$", "MATH_0004": "$\\mathcal{F} \\mapsto \\mathcal{F}(U)$", "MATH_0005": "$\\textit{Ab}(\\mathcal{C}) \\to \\textit{Ab}$", "MATH_0006": "$H^p(U, \\mathcal{F}) = 0$", "MATH_0007": "$\\mathcal{F}$", "MATH_0008": "$p \\geq 1$", "MATH_0009": "$\\mathcal{G}$", "MATH_0010": "$\\mathcal{G}$", "MATH_0011": "$U$", "STRUCT_0001": "\\begin{enumerate}", "STRUCT_0002": "\\item", "STRUCT_0003": "\\item", "STRUCT_0004": "\\item", "STRUCT_0005": "\\end{enumerate}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-w-contractible}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:b9ddaf1f069bcc5022a53a2160f6ad0558c5bdf3d496943d841e7dc00d509b7a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:9c08797ddd8fc9950132c017be26d3369da8a6d4046a305c065c9ac8382715e7", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a site. Let <MATH_0002> be a weakly contractible\nobject of <MATH_0003>. Then\n<STRUCT_0001>\n<STRUCT_0002> the functor <MATH_0004> is an exact\nfunctor <MATH_0005>,\n<STRUCT_0003> <MATH_0006>\nfor every abelian sheaf <MATH_0007> and all <MATH_0008>, and\n<STRUCT_0004> for any sheaf of groups <MATH_0009> any <MATH_0010>-torsor\nhas a section over <MATH_0011>.\n<STRUCT_0005>\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:bd35864031d8793a13551a341d68d82670278ad3dd0fd28689c90eddf337ebfc", "unit_id": "tag:0946:statement"}
{"chapter": "sites-cohomology", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "0945", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$\\mathcal{F}$", "MATH_0002": "$\\mathcal{G}$", "MATH_0003": "$\\mathcal{F} \\to *$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{homology-section-functors}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{derived-lemma-right-derived-exact-functor}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:02c3f2144084ff75c531ad3df1a9d1cd2f64fdb98d5bef3a62ced34335dffd07", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:3528da766eed8120b9124508fbefcf6a7c52c498d40dc88702781cc79a7712bc", "source_text": "The first statement follows immediately from the definition\n(see also Homology, Section <REF_0001>).\nThe higher derived functors vanish by\nDerived Categories, Lemma <REF_0002>.\nLet <MATH_0001> be a <MATH_0002>-torsor. Then <MATH_0003>\nis a surjective map of sheaves. Hence (3) follows from the\ndefinition as well.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:d32c0316b0dc0f893b583956195887c642c7f7cab2afcadd1927b580374b12ca", "unit_id": "tag:0946:proof"}
{"chapter": "sites-cohomology", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "0945", "placeholders": {"STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:bfb608957d3c59da09f8d940848457245c8e6ea179342f5bee55999c3d353002", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nIt is convenient to list some consequences of having enough\nweakly contractible objects here.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:e8f9ff5b436dd9c1e131e092491aa4530a35a39aa3df99c59965a6a4a3dc8017", "unit_id": "tag:0945:prose-0002"}
